  ⚠️ When `single` is `"false"`, several answers have a `fraction` > 0. The sum of the positive fractions must be 100.
  ```json
  {
    "type": "multichoice",
    "content": {
      "name": "Q02 - Renewable energy",
      "questiontext": "Among the following energy sources, which are renewable?",
      "feedback": "Solar, wind and hydropower are renewable energies.",
      "single": "false",
      "correctfeedback": "Well done, all the correct answers are ticked!",
      "partiallycorrectfeedback": "Some answers are correct, but not all.",
      "incorrectfeedback": "No correct answer selected.",
      "answers": [
        { "text": "Solar energy", "fraction": 33.33333, "feedback": "Yes: the Sun's radiation is continuously renewed." },
        { "text": "Wind energy", "fraction": 33.33333, "feedback": "Yes: wind is an inexhaustible resource." },
        { "text": "Hydropower", "fraction": 33.33334, "feedback": "Yes: moving water is renewed thanks to the water cycle." },
        { "text": "Nuclear energy", "fraction": 0, "feedback": "Nuclear power depends on uranium, an exhaustible resource: it is not renewable." },
        { "text": "Oil", "fraction": 0, "feedback": "Oil is a fossil fuel available in limited quantities: it is not renewable." }
      ]
    }
  }
  ```

- **For the `matching` type (Matching):**
  ⚠️ The `text` field is rendered as HTML (LaTeX OK), but `answer` is displayed in a drop-down menu (Unicode only, NEVER LaTeX).
